sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant O as Owner of one guest command
  participant L as Leader (bash), held unreaped
  participant G as Rest of the owned group
  participant W as Capture worker
  Note over O: T0 - the owner chose timed_out or cancelled
  O->>L: SIGTERM to the group (killpg while L is unreaped)
  O->>G: same SIGTERM reaches every member
  alt leader exits by T0 + 1.9 s
    L-->>O: exit status event, no reap yet
  else no exit by T0 + 1.9 s
    Note over O: grace ends
  end
  Note over O: K - SIGKILL, still before the reap
  O->>L: SIGKILL to the group
  O->>G: same SIGKILL reaches every member
  alt exit status arrives by K + 1.4 s
    L-->>O: exit status (termination.leaderStatus)
    O->>L: reap the leader
    loop signal-0 probe until ESRCH or K + 1.4 s
      O->>G: kill(-pgid, 0)
    end
    Note over O,G: ESRCH gives groupEmpty yes. Members at K + 1.4 s give no. EPERM gives unknown.
  else no exit status by K + 1.4 s
    Note over O,L: leaderStatus unavailable, groupEmpty no.<br/>The owner holds L, reaps it later<br/>and sends no further signal.
  end
  O->>W: read each file from offset 0 up to fileBytes
  W-->>O: complete streams by K + 1.9 s
  Note over O,W: A stream not read by K + 1.9 s is an incomplete prefix with reason deadline.
  Note over O: publish the record. withinBounds is derived: groupEmpty yes, K at most 2 s, record at most 2 s after K.
